A</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>YAMAGUCHI, KATSUMI</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A modifier which comprises a blend of an impact modifier and a polymeric processability modifier in a weight ratio of 95/5 to 80/20 and in which a 0.4 wt.% toluene solution of the polymeric processability modifier has a specific viscosity as measured at 30  DEG C of 2.5 to 5.0. It imparts impact resistance and high transparency to methacrylic resins processed under a wide range of conditions.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention concerne un adjuvant qui comprend un mélange d'un modificateur d'impact et un modificateur de transformabilité polymère avec un taux de poids compris entre 95 / 5 et 80 / 20, dans lequel une solution de toluène de 0,4 % possède une viscosité spécifique, mesurée à 30  DEG C, de 2,5 à 5,0. L'adjuvant de l'invention confère une résistance à l'impact et une transparence élevée aux résines méthacryliques dans les conditions les plus variées.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>